NAME
    readc - read one character or terminal key from the controlling terminal

SYNOPSIS
    readc

DESCRIPTION
    readc is a standalone POSIX-shell terminal reader. It reads one key from
    /dev/tty, using terminfo for terminal key sequences, and restores the
    terminal state before returning.

    Named keys such as arrows, Home, End, Insert, Delete, PageUp/PageDown,
    function keys, Enter, Backspace, Tab and Escape are written as symbolic
    names. Printable ASCII and valid UTF-8 characters are written directly.

    The current implementation defines no command-line options.

EXIT STATUS
    0   A supported key or character was read.
    1   Terminal, terminfo or I/O/setup failure.
    2   Unsupported, invalid or incomplete input.
